# System-wide msmtp config, installed by deploy.sh to /etc/msmtprc
# (world-readable; see below for why that is safe). Used by
# scripts/lib.sh's notify() to send review-queue emails via Fastmail SMTP.
#
# This file holds no secret. The SMTP password is fetched at send time via
# passwordeval, which reads $MUSICBOX_SMTP_PASSWORD from msmtp's own process
# environment rather than re-reading /etc/musicbox/env from disk. That
# variable is already present there because music-import's systemd unit
# carries EnvironmentFile=/etc/musicbox/env (root:root 0600): systemd loads
# the file as root at service start and injects every NAME=value line into
# the started (music-owned) process's environment, which msmtp then
# inherits as a child of that process. Having passwordeval open the file a
# second time would need /etc/musicbox/env made group-readable by "music",
# which would hand that same unprivileged process direct read access to
# every OTHER secret in the file (R2 keys, the tunnel token) too — no
# smaller a blast radius than the inherited-env-var it already carries, so
# there is nothing to gain and a real permission bit to lose.
# Port 587 with STARTTLS, not 465 implicit TLS: Hetzner Cloud blocks
# outbound 25 and 465 by default on new accounts (confirmed from the box
# 2026-08-31: both time out, 587 connects). Fastmail serves the same
# authenticated submission on 587.
defaults
tls on
tls_starttls on
tls_trust_file /etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt
logfile /srv/music/state/msmtp.log

account fastmail
host smtp.fastmail.com
port 587
auth on
user geoff-login@907.life
from geoff-login@907.life
passwordeval "printenv MUSICBOX_SMTP_PASSWORD"

account default : fastmail
